# {pkg_name}

Self-contained Lumis language package for {languages_text}.

The Tree-sitter parser is compiled to WASM and ships with the queries that highlight it.

Built with [`tree-sitter build --wasm`](https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter/cli/build.html) `v{tree_sitter_cli_version}`

Used by [Lumis](https://lumis.sh) and compatible with [web-tree-sitter](https://www.npmjs.com/package/web-tree-sitter) v{tree_sitter_cli} and other WASM runtimes.

## Installation

```sh
npm install {pkg_name}
```

## What it contains

`{wasm_name}.wasm` is the parser. `lumis.json` describes it and records its size, its SHA-256 and the queries.

Lumis reads both from the installed package, so nothing is downloaded at runtime.

The only JavaScript here is one line that exports the parser's URL, for bundlers that want it.

## Parser

| Parser | Version | Rev |
| ------ | ------- | --- |
| [{git_url}]({git_url}) | {upstream_version} | {rev} |

The same parser is published to Hex as
[`{hex_package}`](https://hex.pm/packages/{hex_package}) — byte for byte, from
one build, so both registries serve the same artifact.

